🛠️ Week 1: Secure Transport & Authentication Setup
Goal: Secure the gRPC channel between the central orchestrator and hospital client nodes using Mutual TLS (mTLS).

Day 1 — Research & Design
Analysed the cross-silo FL threat model: untrusted network, rogue hospital nodes, MITM risk.
Outlined communication security requirements: confidentiality, mutual authentication, integrity.
Set up the security/ and scripts/ directory structures.
Documented cipher suite requirements: TLS 1.3 only, ECDHE key exchange.
Day 2 — Library Selection
Selected the cryptography library (≥ 42) for all PKI primitives — preferred over pyOpenSSL for its modern, Pythonic API.
Selected grpcio (≥ 1.62) for secure channel construction.
Drafted certificate hierarchy: CA → Server Cert → N × Client Cert.
Decided all private key files would be chmod 600; .gitignore'd from the repository.
Day 3 — CA & Key Generation
Implemented CA and server certificate generation using EC keys (NIST P-256), replacing the initial RSA prototype with ECDSA for better performance:

python

# scripts/gen_certs.py — CA generation
ca_key = ec.generate_private_key(ec.SECP256R1(), default_backend())
ca_cert = (
    x509.CertificateBuilder()
    .subject_name(ca_subject)
    .issuer_name(ca_subject)          # self-signed
    .public_key(ca_key.public_key())
    .serial_number(x509.random_serial_number())
    .add_extension(x509.BasicConstraints(ca=True, path_length=None), critical=True)
    .sign(ca_key, hashes.SHA256(), backend)
)
Day 4 — Client Certs & Credential Helpers
Created build_client_cert() — signs N client certs under the CA, each embedding ExtendedKeyUsage.CLIENT_AUTH.
Implemented credential loader helpers in 
security/grpc_tls.py
:
python

# security/grpc_tls.py — bundle credentials for the gRPC server
def load_server_credentials(cert_dir, *, require_client_auth=True):
    return grpc.ssl_server_credentials(
        private_key_certificate_chain_pairs=[(server_key, server_cert)],
        root_certificates=ca_cert,
        require_client_auth=require_client_auth,   # enforces mTLS
    )
Added verify_cert_chain() and is_cert_expired() utilities for offline validation.
